    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        0,
        820
      ],
      "size": [
        760,
        520
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 2,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "SDXL Outpaint + Upscale (Image Recall)\n\n1. Drop a PNG onto the Image Recall node (on the node, NOT the empty canvas, which would load the PNG's own workflow). The box under it shows the checkpoint, LoRAs, prompts and settings it found.\n2. Outpaint Canvas: pick the aspect (16:9, 9:16, 21:9 ...) and where the original sits (center = grow both sides, left = grow to the right).\n3. prompt_prefix is put in front of the recalled prompt: describe the wider scene there (\"wide shot, desert stretching to the horizon\").\n   Main subject: Step 1 uses two prompts. The recalled prompt only covers the original pixels; the new area gets outpaint_positive, where the subject is weighted down so it isn't painted again (no duplicate cat above its head). subject = the main object ('cat'); empty = first part of the prompt; 'none' = off. subject_weight: 0.4 = faint hint, 0 = removed. The info box shows the 'Outpaint area prompt'.\n4. Queue. Three steps run:\n   Step 1 - Outpaint: fills the new area at SDXL size (~1MP) with the image's own sampler settings, then pastes the original pixels back. Costs one normal render.\n   Step 2 - Upscale: RealESRGAN x4, then resize to the exact ratio (16:9 x2 = 2688x1512). Fast.\n   Step 3 - Tiled Refine: re-details the big image in 1024px tiles. 2688x1512 = 6 tiles; each tile costs like one SDXL render at Step 3's step count (default 10 steps, dpmpp_2m: about one Step 1 in total).\n\nSpeed on 8 GB\n- Many LoRAs make every step much slower. Untick apply_loras for a quick test.\n- Fast draft: select Step 3 and press Ctrl+B to bypass it.\n- Don't give Step 3 a *_2s_* or sde sampler: they cost 2 model calls per step.\n\nTuning\n- Step 3 denoise: 0.2 stays close to the upscale, 0.4 adds more detail (and more change). Seams: raise overlap to 192.\n- Seam between old and new area: raise feather on Outpaint Canvas.\n- Subject still repeats: lower subject_weight to 0, or type the subject words in 'subject' (e.g. 'cat, kitten').\n- New area ignores the scene: write more in prompt_prefix, or set prompt_override.\n- Missing checkpoint/LoRA: shown with ! in the info box; pick a checkpoint by hand."
      ],
      "title": "How to use",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
